@startuml 04-sequence-task-lifecycle
title FlowAI Platform - Task Lifecycle (sequence)

autonumber

participant "Automation" as Auto
participant "Operator (UI)" as U
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Event Router" as ER
participant "Secret Service" as SS
participant "Executor" as EX
participant "Agent Container" as AG
participant "LLM Provider" as LLM

note over Auto, U
  GW is an auth-aware reverse proxy. Its only logic is:
  (1) validate auth, (2) route to a backend service,
  (3) return the backend's response.
  No business logic. No state. No writes.
  Automation bypasses GW and calls ER directly with a token.
  All writes and process logic happen in backend services (ER, SS, EX).
end note

== Submit (automation -> ER direct) ==

Auto -> GW : POST /auth/login
GW --> Auto : 200 { bearer_token }
Auto -> ER : REST POST /tasks (bearer_token, prompt, tools, secret_ids)
ER -> SS : REST open env (validate secret_ids exist)
SS --> ER : ok
ER -> ER : Build scope (HMAC: project, task, secret_ids, TTL)
ER -> ER : Persist task (status=queued, scope_token, routing_target) in ER DB
ER --> Auto : 202 task_id

== Subscribe (UI -> GW -> ER) ==

U -> GW : WS connect (bearer_token)
GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
GW -> ER : REST subscribe to task_id events (bearer_token)
ER -> GW : subscription ack
GW -> U : WS upgrade ack

== Dispatch (ER dispatches via REST) ==

ER -> ER : Pick next pending task from ER DB
ER -> EX : REST POST /dispatch { task_spec + scope_token }
EX -> SS : REST open env { scope_token }
SS --> EX : env-style keys
EX -> EX : Pull image
EX -> AG : Start container, mount secrets as env / tmpfs

note over AG, EX
  Agent is a black box. Runs initial instructions. No platform API.
end note

AG -> LLM : Prompt + history
LLM --> AG : Completion or tool_use

== Agent loop (event fanout via REST) ==

loop agent loop
  AG --> EX : stdout (event stream)
  EX -> ER : REST POST /events { task_id, kind, payload }
  ER -> ER : Persist event in ER DB
  ER -> GW : REST push (event to subscribers)
  GW -> U : WS push (live)

  opt Operator intervenes
    U -> GW : inject message / cancel / rerun (WS frame, bearer_token)
    GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
    GW -> ER : REST POST /control { task_id, action }
    ER -> EX : REST POST /control { task_id, action }
    EX --> AG : forward (or stop)
  end

  AG -> LLM : Next prompt
  LLM --> AG : Next completion
end

== Finalize ==

AG --> EX : final result (stdout / exit code)
EX -> ER : REST POST /events { status=terminal, result }
ER -> ER : UPDATE task status to terminal in ER DB
ER -> GW : REST push (final event)
GW -> U : WS final
ER --> Auto : callback (if configured)

note over AG, EX
  Container terminated. Scope token expires.
end note

@enduml